# STAGED base .cursorignore — the RELIABLE read boundary for the open-door harness.
# Research R2: beforeReadFile deny is unreliable; .cursorignore + sandbox protected paths are
# the real read wall. This file is UNIVERSAL (every door) — it hides secret/credential material
# from the agent entirely, regardless of active door.
#
# ACTIVATION: copy to the workspace root as `.cursorignore` (per-repo) and/or merge into
#   ~/.cursorignore. It is NOT auto-installed by this phase. Copying it only hides files; it
#   cannot wedge a session (reversible: delete the entries).

# --- Credentials / secrets — NO DOOR EVER (SSOT §2, doors-v1 universal_rules.secrets_infisical) ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/keys.env
**/secrets/**
**/*secret*
**/*credential*
**/credentials*
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.ssh/**
**/.aws/**
**/.gnupg/**
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
.amplified/keys.env
.amplified/*.env
.vellum/*.env

# --- Cursor / git internals the sandbox also protects (belt-and-braces) ---
**/.git/config
**/.git/hooks/**

# --- High-noise / non-source (token hygiene; complements token-efficiency.mdc) ---
**/node_modules/**
**/dist/**
**/build/**
**/.next/**
**/coverage/**
**/vendor/**
**/*.min.js
**/*.map
**/.venv/**
**/__pycache__/**
**/.pytest_cache/**
**/target/**

# --- Per-door add-ons (recommended; uncomment in a door-scoped .cursorignore) ---
# research_read: nothing extra — broadest read door.
# agentsmini_build / worktree_feature: add sibling projects you are NOT working in, e.g.
#   /Users/ewansair/other-project/**
# central_handoff: add non-handoff estate trees you do not need to read here.
